          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தேவை — tēvai — \"a need; a requirement\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மக்களின் தேவைகளை அரசு கவனிக்க வேண்டும். makkaḷiṉ tēvaikaḷai aracu kavaṉikka vēṇṭum. The government must attend to the needs of the people."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: தேவைகள், tēvaikaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எனக்கு ஒரு புத்தகம் தேவை (tēvai), I need a book: the person in the dative. தேவையில்லை, there is no need."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தேவை (tēvai) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3469 lists Tamil tēvai, \"affairs; compelling need, necessity\", with Malayalam tēva, \"need\"."
            }
          ]
